vow 1 component orders_reader
# archvow vow of orders_reader - what it must be and do; archvow check holds the code to it.
# Read: archvow show orders_reader. Change: archvow specify orders_reader. Never edit by hand.
name orders
type reader
kind files
layer p2_io
module my_pipeline.p2_io.orders_reader
ticket US-001
description "Read the orders from CSV files with a header at the given path and enforce ORDERS_SCHEMA"
uses [orders_schema]

# --- symbols
symbol read_orders
  kind function
  signature "(spark: SparkSession, path: str) -> DataFrame"

# --- decisions
decision 1
  question "The path does not exist or is empty (e.g. today's file was not delivered): fail or return an empty DataFrame?"
  answer "Fail with a clear error: a missing input is an operations problem"
  by architect@example.com
  on 2026-11-11T19:06:56.526320+00:00

decision 2
  question "Rows that do not match the schema (wrong type, missing column) - e.g. amount = \"abc\": stop the job, drop them, or set them aside in a reject file (where)?"
  answer "Fail the job (FAILFAST): a malformed file must be fixed upstream"
  by architect@example.com
  on 2026-11-11T19:06:56.749135+00:00

decision 3
  question "On each run, what does it read: everything at the path, or only one date (e.g. the folder date=2026-10-12)? If that date's data is not there yet: fail, wait, or read the previous date?"
  answer "Everything under the given path, no partitions"
  by architect@example.com
  on 2026-11-11T19:06:57.015876+00:00

decision 4
  question "Does an approved shared library already read these files (e.g. acme_io.read_csv, listed in requirements.txt)? Then the code calls it - which function - instead of reading them with Spark."
  answer "No: Spark reads it itself"
  by architect@example.com
  on 2026-11-11T19:06:57.244572+00:00

assumptions []

# --- hazards
hazard H1
  guide_word missing
  severity high
  never "an absent, empty or late input is processed as if it were complete"
  by architect@example.com
  on 2026-11-11T19:07:08.397973+00:00

hazard H2
  guide_word wrong
  severity high
  never "a null, negative or out-of-range value reaches the output"
  by architect@example.com
  on 2026-11-11T19:07:08.875814+00:00

hazard H3
  guide_word stale
  severity medium
  never "old data is processed as if it were current"
  by architect@example.com
  on 2026-11-11T19:07:09.163482+00:00

